# Generated output: the compiled thesis is tracked so that PDF changes are reviewable in git.
# Everything else latexmk writes into that directory stays out.
output/pdf/*
!output/pdf/thesis.pdf

# Figure sources: the matplotlib figures build inside a local virtualenv created by
# figures/src/build.sh from figures/src/requirements.txt. The environment and the
# screen-resolution PNG preview are byproducts; the vector PDF in figures/ is tracked.
.env/
.venv/
figures/src/.venv/
figures/src/*.png

# Reference vault: the PDFs themselves are not committed (size and publisher licences).
# references/MANIFEST.tsv is committed, so the record of what was checked survives.
references/pdf/
references/.manifest.lock

# The root thesis.pdf is a tracked symlink to output/pdf/thesis.pdf, not a second copy. Git
# stores the link itself, so a clone resolves it against the tracked build output. Do not
# ignore it, and do not replace it with a regular file.

/tmp
